    },
    {
      "id": "152f1aa193ff8ab99e94be535847b3e936a13c46",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 535605137,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi Anders\n\nThanks for your comment and approving my other changes.\n\n\"dissector_handle_t field_dissector = (field_full_name && (subdissect_all_pbf_types || field_type == PROTOBUF_TYPE_BYTES || field_type == PROTOBUF_TYPE_STRING)) ?\n        dissector_get_string_handle(protobuf_field_subdissector_table, field_full_name) : NULL;\"\n\nIf plugin dissector is allowed to register for all fields, it will cause a hash lookup for every protobuf field.\nso, probably, to avoid too many hash lookups the original author limited plugin dissectors for byte and string types only, which would need a plugin dissector mostly.\nMy change provides a preference option, in case registering plugin dissector is required for other types.\n\nIf frequent hash lookup is not an issue, I dont see any reason for protobuf field type checks before lookup.\n\nRegards\nRanjeet S",
          "author": {
            "id": 8400999,
            "username": "ranjeetsih",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Ranjeet Kumar Singh",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d8e2f674adfc2cd2f3707f8de3107baa06721440424842b13308eaef5650052e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/ranjeetsih"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-23T11:11:46.478Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-23T11:12:21.287Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 92838464,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
